; The library a game opens, and the only one it should have to. In React's terms
; this is react-dom; camlcast.core is the DOM and camlcast.loom is React.
;
; The module named for the library is the library: dune makes camlcast.ml the
; interface and everything beside it reachable only through what that file
; chooses to re-export. That turns the boundary from a convention into a fact
; the compiler enforces — Engine, Renderer, Framebuffer, World and Player are
; not re-exported, so autocomplete cannot surface them.
;
; The only library depending on both of the others, and deliberately the only
; one: loom knows nothing of walls, core knows nothing of components, and
; everything that has to know both is here.

(library
 (name camlcast)
 (public_name camlcast)
 (libraries camlcast_core camlcast_loom))
